---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import InsightCallout from '../../components/InsightCallout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/SectionHeading.astro';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="ClearCase"
  description="ClearCase is a fully automated cartridge case triage solution for crime gun investigations. The product worked technically, but it had been built to prove a concept, not to support how investigators work in practice. I led a full UX/UI redesign to fix that, and in the process uncovered a critical gap in the workflow."
  tags={['B2B SaaS', 'Forensics', 'Responsive Web']}
  heroImage="/images/projects/clearcase/thumbnail.png"
  accentColor="#2c3e50"
  previousProject={{ title: 'Deposify', slug: 'deposify' }}
  nextProject={{ title: 'LeadSuite', slug: 'leadsuite' }}
>
  <div class="case-study-body">

    <!-- Challenge -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="The Challenge"
          subtitle="ClearCase worked. The automated analysis was accurate and investigators could pull results. But the product had been built to a prototype standard: no design system, no responsive layout, and no real consideration for how law enforcement agencies operate day to day. The interface was dense, hard to navigate, and hadn't been designed around how investigators move through a case. A full redesign was needed before ClearCase could be something agencies would genuinely adopt."
        />
        <p class="design-question"><strong>Design Question:</strong> How do you turn a technically capable but workflow-unaware tool into a product investigators actually trust?</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Before state -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="img-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16/9;" data-label="Before - read-only web app state · 16:9"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Redesign -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="The Redesign"
          subtitle="I redesigned ClearCase from the ground up, aligning it with the LeadsOnline design system to give it consistency with the broader platform investigators already used. Navigation, layout, and visual language were rebuilt to match how agencies operate in the field, not how the original prototype assumed they would. The redesign is fully responsive and built to scale."
        />
        <div class="img-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16/9;" data-label="Redesigned navigation and layouts · 16:9"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- A Gap Surfaces -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="A Gap Surfaces"
          subtitle="As the redesign took shape and we gathered feedback from investigators, a bigger problem became clear. The web app had no way to add exhibits. Every exhibit had to be created on mobile, which meant the phone wasn't just a companion device, it was the only real entry point to the workflow. Agencies were hesitant to rely on mobile for core casework, and the redesigned web app, however much improved, still left investigators at a dead end the moment they needed to act on what they found."
        />
        <div class="img-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 4/3;" data-label="Workflow mapping / gap analysis artifact · 4:3"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Web-Based Exhibit Creation -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Web-Based Exhibit Creation"
          subtitle="The new web-based exhibit workflow makes the desktop app the primary place investigators create and process exhibits, instead of forcing them to work solely from their phone. In collaboration with engineering, we designed a compliant flow that uses the phone's NFC reader without storing anything locally, easing agencies' concerns around mobile use. The result is an intuitive, web-first experience that directly addresses the core pain point investigators had with the original workflow."
        />
        <div class="img-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16/9;" data-label="Exhibit creation flow · 16:9"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Reflection -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading title="Reflection" />
        <div class="reflections-grid">
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>Design surfaces what's missing</h3>
            <p>The redesign process wasn't just about polish. Mapping real workflows and gathering investigator feedback surfaced the exhibit creation gap that wasn't visible until we looked closely at how the product was being used. The redesign created the conditions for that discovery.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>System as accelerator</h3>
            <p>Building on the LeadsOnline design system meant ClearCase felt native to the platform from day one. Shared tokens, components, and patterns cut design time significantly and gave the redesign a coherence it would have taken much longer to achieve from scratch.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>From prototype to product</h3>
            <p>ClearCase went from a technically capable prototype to a product agencies could genuinely adopt. The redesign addressed both the surface-level UX issues and the underlying workflow gaps that had made it hard to rely on.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</CaseStudyLayout>

<style>
  .design-question {
    font-size: var(--text-body-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .design-question strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .reflections-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .reflections-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .reflection-item h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-h4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .reflection-item p {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  /* Placeholder image scaffolding */
  .img-placeholder {
    width: 100%;
    background-color: var(--color-surface);
    border: 2px dashed var(--color-text-muted);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .img-placeholder::after {
    content: attr(data-label);
    position: absolute;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    text-align: center;
    padding: var(--space-md);
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { initCaseStudyAnimations } from '../../scripts/scroll-animations';
  initCaseStudyAnimations('.case-section');
</script>
